ion, candidate label generation, and candidate label ranking.", "node_id": "029e3ab3a51308dfb0d5", "support_score": 0.9697, "context_id": "C4"}, {"claim": "During sense disambiguation, each word in the cluster is assigned to a WordNet synset by choosing the set of synsets (S*) that minimizes the total WordNet pathwise distance between them.", "node_id": "029e3ab3a51308dfb0d5", "support_score": 0.4929, "context_id": "C4"}, {"claim": "In candidate label generation, a set of possible labels (L) is created by taking the union of all hypernyms of the chosen synsets in S*.", "node_id": "029e3ab3a51308dfb0d5", "support_score": 0.9861, "context_id": "C4"}, {"claim": "In candidate label ranking, candidate label synsets in L are scored by the sum of their WordNet pathwise distances to each synset in S* and ranked from least to most distance.", "node_id": "029e3ab3a51308dfb0d5", "support_score": 0.8889, "context_id": "C4"}], "system": "learned_v5"}
